WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.115
Followers are vanity.

00:00:01.115 --> 00:00:03.344
Conversations are the score that teaches.

00:00:03.344 --> 00:00:05.944
This lesson is about your first scoreboard.

00:00:05.944 --> 00:00:07.059
Conversations > followers.

00:00:07.059 --> 00:00:09.660
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.375
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:13.375 --> 00:00:18.948
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:18.948 --> 00:00:23.034
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:23.034 --> 00:00:27.864
Stay practical: create a one-line weekly scoreboard before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.184 --> 00:00:33.649
Your first scoreboard is one line: conversations started, offers made, money asked, lessons shipped.

00:00:33.649 --> 00:00:36.772
Remember the objective: create a one-line weekly scoreboard.

00:00:36.772 --> 00:00:41.067
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:45.751
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.751 --> 00:00:50.045
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:50.045 --> 00:00:54.730
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:57.462
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:57.462 --> 00:00:59.024
Feedback beats guessing alone.

